  "description_html": "Diagram featuring all the current named Dinosauria from the Bayan Shireh Formation. Dinosaur taxa:\n<ul><li><i>Achillobator giganticus</i> → Burkhant locality. Length = 5 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Amtocephale gobiensis</i> → Amtgai locality. Length = Extrapolated after relatives.</li>\n<li><i>Enigmosaurus mongoliensis</i> → Khara Khutul locality. Length = 5 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Erketu ellisoni</i> → Bor Guvé locality. Length = 15 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Paul2016_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Paul2016-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Erlikosaurus andrewsi</i> → Bayshin Tsav locality. Length = 3.2 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-2\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Duonychus tsogtbaatari</i> → Urlibe Khudak locality. Length = Similar to <i>Erlikosaurus</i>,<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> 3 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Garudimimus brevipes</i> → Bayshin Tsav locality. Length = ∼3.5 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-5\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Gobihadros mongoliensis</i> → Bayshin Tsav, Baynshire, Char Teeg, Khongil Tsav, Khoorai Tsav localities. Length = 7.5 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-6\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-6\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Graciliceratops mongoliensis</i> → Sheeregeen Gashoon locality. Length = ∼60 centimeters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Khankhuuluu mongoliensis</i> → Bayshin Tsav locality. Length = 5 meters,<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-4\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> 1.2 meters at the hips.<sup id=\"cite_ref-7\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-7\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Segnosaurus galbinensis</i> → Amtgai, Bayshin Tsav, Khara Khutul, Ulribe Khuduk localities. Length = 7 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-8\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Talarurus plicatospineus</i> → Bayshin Tsav, Baynshire, Shine Us Khuduk localities. Length = 5 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-5\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Tsagantegia longicranialis</i> → Tsagan Teg locality. Length = 6 meters.<sup id=\"cite_ref-9\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-9\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<p>Excluded taxa:\n</p>\n<ul><li><i>Amtosaurus magnus</i> is known from a partial braincase and is considered as an invalid taxon.<sup id=\"cite_ref-10\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-10\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li><i>Maleevus disparoserratus</i> has very sparce remains and is considered as an invalid taxon.<sup id=\"cite_ref-11\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-11\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li>\n<li>\"Gallimimus mongoliensis\" is likely a distinct ornithomimid from the actual <i>Gallimimus</i>, but remains undescribed.<sup id=\"cite_ref-12\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-12\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup></li></ul>\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-Holtz2012-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-0\"><sup><i><b>a</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-1\"><sup><i><b>b</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-2\"><sup><i><b>c</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-3\"><sup><i><b>d</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-4\"><sup><i><b>e</b></i></sup></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Holtz2012_1-5\"><sup><i><b>f</b></i></sup></a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">(2007) <i> Dinosaurs: The Most Complete, Up-to-Date Encyclopedia for Dinosaur Lovers of All Ages</i>, Random House  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/9780375824197\" title=\"Special:BookSources/9780375824197\">9780375824197</a>. </small></cite> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.geol.umd.edu/~tholtz/dinoappendix/HoltzappendixWinter2011.pdf\">Genus List for Holtz 2012</a>  <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.geol.umd.edu/~tholtz/dinoappendix/appendix.html\">Weight Information</a></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-Paul2016-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Paul2016_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite class=\"book\" style=\"font-style:normal\">(2016) <i> The Princeton Field Guide to Dinosaurs</i> (2nd ed.), <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/en:Princeton,_New_Jersey\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:en:Princeton, New Jersey\"><span title=\"municipality in Mercer County, New Jersey, United States\">Princeton</span></a>:  Princeton University Press, pp. 162−168  <small><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISBN\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">ISBN</span></a></span>:  <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/9780691167664\" title=\"Special:BookSources/9780691167664\">9780691167664</a>. </small></cite></span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><cite style=\"font-style:normal\">(in english) (2025). \"<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12131255\">Didactyl therizinosaur with a preserved keratinous claw from the Late Cretaceous of Mongolia</a>\". <i>iScience</i> <b>28</b> (4). <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_object_identifier\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Digital object identifier\">DOI</a></span>:<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.isci.2025.112141\">10.1016/j.isci.2025.112141</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PubMed_Central\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:PubMed Central\"><span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\">PMC</span></a></span>: <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12131255\">12131255</a>. <span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISSN\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:ISSN\"><span lang=\"en\